# lightweight-rec configuration.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/record/config and uncomment what you need. skhd does not
# load your shell rc, so Option+R sees this file and nothing else.
#
# Plain shell assignments, one per line: `record` sources this file, so a syntax
# error here breaks the hotkey. Every key below is optional and shows its
# default. The same list, with the detail, is the Configuration table in the
# README.
#
# Only RECORD_DIR is destructive: every start deletes this tool's own mp4 files
# older than RECORD_DAYS at its top level, so give it a directory of its own.
# The install-time flags (--with-blackhole, --with-handy) go on the ./install.sh
# command line, never in here.

# Where the mp4 files, the logs and the whisper model live.
# RECORD_DIR="$HOME/Recordings"

# Root of your Obsidian vault: the folder that has a .obsidian directory in it.
# RECORD_VAULT="$HOME/Documents/Obsidian"

# Folder the note is filed in. Outside a vault, the stop warns you and says where.
# RECORD_NOTES="$RECORD_VAULT/Recordings"

# Display to capture, as an ffmpeg avfoundation index. List them: record screens
# RECORD_SCREEN=0

# Microphone by device name; empty resolves one on every start. It decides on
# every path, BlackHole included. Check it with: record-audio which
# RECORD_MIC=""

# 0 turns off BlackHole full-call audio: the microphone alone, no aggregates.
# RECORD_SYSTEM_AUDIO=1

# 0 never calls the claude CLI: no egress, no title, tags, summary or screen text.
# RECORD_CLAUDE=1

# Retention in days for this tool's own mp4 files in RECORD_DIR.
# RECORD_DAYS=14

# App to open once the capture is up, by its name. Empty opens nothing.
# RECORD_LAUNCH_APP=""

# The red dot overlay, if you moved it out of ~/bin.
# RECORD_DOT="$HOME/bin/record-dot"

# The CoreAudio helper, if you moved it out of ~/bin.
# RECORD_AUDIO="$HOME/bin/record-audio"

# The config file itself: read from the environment, so setting it here does nothing.
# RECORD_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/record/config"
